# secrets
.env
.env.*
!sample.env

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache/

# generated audio + episode output (keep the dir, ignore contents)
.render-cache/
# Pristine copies of an episode's script.json / episode.json / segment PCM, taken by
# scripts/recast_archive.py before it recasts that episode IN PLACE. Same reason episodes/ is
# ignored: it is generated audio and generated JSON, it is large, and it is the safety net for a
# local run rather than part of the project.
.recast-backup/
# Local episode directories that the hosted archive superseded. Six dates held a completely
# different show under the same id as the deployed volume; the live version won, and the local one
# was moved here rather than deleted. Same reason as above: generated audio, large, local only.
.superseded-local-episodes/
# The cast page's per-voice samples, as they were before 2026-08-21, when all 36 were re-rendered
# on one line (scripts/make_cast_samples.py). Kept only so the old reads are recoverable by hand;
# episodes/ is ignored, so these were never committed in the first place.
.superseded-samples/
episodes/*
!episodes/.gitkeep
!episodes/cover.png

# macOS
.DS_Store

# --- Build-time working artifacts: on disk, deliberately not in the repo ---
#
# None of this is deleted. It all still lives in the working copy, and some of it is the raw
# material for the write-ups about this project. What it has in common is that it is about
# BUILDING HN Radio rather than running it, and someone cloning this to see how the show works
# should not have to sort the two apart.
#
# Several of these also carry material that is simply not publishable: imported call summaries
# and Slack captures with named colleagues, internal positioning, and workspace permalinks.
# Nothing under these paths should ever be committed. A pre-commit hook in .githooks/ enforces
# that; see DEPLOY.md if you are setting up a fresh clone.

# Project board, append-only build ledger, imported conversations, and the generated event log.
.hub/

# Git hooks. Local-only tooling: the post-commit event log and the pre-commit guard above.
.githooks/

# Claude Code session state: handoffs, local settings, isolated worktrees.
.claude/

# Specs and plans. Historical: several describe designs the project moved off, so they read as
# current documentation when they are not.
docs/superpowers/

# Point-in-time code review reports. Useful while building, stale the moment they are written.
docs/code-review-*.md
docs/code-review-*.html

# subagent-driven-development scratch (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Hub page generator. Only input is the board, which is not in the repo.
scripts/md_to_hub_page.py

# Derived HTML renders. The markdown next to each one is canonical; DEPLOY.md and glossary.md
# stay tracked and these do not.
docs/*.html
DEPLOY.html
docs/deploy-briefing.md
docs/script-tuning-session.md

# Superseded status surfaces, replaced by the board and never updated after 2026-08-03.
PROGRESS.md
PROGRESS.html
ROADMAP.html
OPEN-ITEMS.html

# Redundant with sample.env, which is the fuller and more current of the two. Shipping both left a
# reader to guess which one to copy.
.env.example
